🔐 Auth Flow (OTP Login with Redis + RabbitMQ)

This project uses OTP-based authentication where the login process is divided into fast user response and background processing using Redis and RabbitMQ.

⚡ Redis (In-Memory Database)

Redis is used for temporary data storage:

Stores OTP with expiry (5 minutes)
Stores rate limit key (60 seconds) to prevent spam
Very fast because data is stored in memory
📦 RabbitMQ (Message Broker)

RabbitMQ is used to handle background tasks asynchronously:

Instead of sending email directly, backend pushes a message to a queue
A separate mail service consumes the queue and sends the email
Improves performance and scalability
🔄 Login Flow
User sends login request with email
Backend checks rate limit in Redis
→ If already requested recently → block request
Generate 6-digit OTP
Store OTP in Redis (expires in 5 minutes)
Set rate limit key in Redis (expires in 60 seconds)
Send OTP email task to RabbitMQ queue (send-otp)
Backend immediately responds: "OTP sent"
📨 Mail Service (Consumer Flow)
Listens to send-otp queue
Receives message (email + OTP)
Sends email using Nodemailer
Acknowledges message (ack) → removes it from queue
🧠 Key Concepts
Redis → Fast temporary storage (OTP, rate limit)
RabbitMQ → Background job processing (email sending)
assertQueue → Ensure queue exists
sendToQueue → Add message to queue
consume → Process messages from queue
ack → Confirm task completion
🎯 Overall Idea

User gets a fast response, while heavy work (email sending) runs in the background.
